### Casos de prueba

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.- Flujo completo: registro → login → crear evento → inscribirse → consultar mis tickets → cancelar
### Creamos 5 usuarios. 2 users, 2 organizers y 1 admin 
### (organizer y admin seran asignados directamente por la base de datos)
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/register 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "user1",
    "last_name": "bot1",
    "email": "user1@gmail.com",
    "password": "user1_1234",
    "role": "puedo poner cualquier cosa, se asigna role:'user' por defecto"
}
###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/register 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "user2",
    "last_name": "bot2",
    "email": "user2@gmail.com",
    "password": "user2_1234"
}
###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/register 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "orzanizer1",
    "last_name": "org1",
    "email": "organizer1@gmail.com",
    "password": "organizer1_1234"
}
###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/register 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "organizer2",
    "last_name": "org2",
    "email": "organizer2@gmail.com",
    "password": "organizer2_1234"
}
###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/register 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "Leandro",
    "last_name": "Meier",
    "email": "leandromeier@gmail.com",
    "password": "admin1234",
    "role": "puedo poner cualquier cosa, se asigna role:'user' por defecto"
}

### Nos registramos como un organizador
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "organizer1@gmail.com",
    "password": "organizer1_1234"
}

### Creamos un evento:
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "evento 1",
    "description": "descripcion del evento 1",
    "category": "categoria 1",
    "date": "2027-01-01",
    "location": "ubicacion 1",
    "capacity": 100,
    "price": 10
}
### Hacemos logout e iniciamos sesión con un usuario
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/logout

###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "user2@gmail.com",
    "password": "user2_1234"
}

### Nos inscribimos a un evento
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events/6ac96c5de8902df7496e38da/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "quantity": 4
}

### Consultar mis tickets
GET http://localhost:9909/api/tickets/my-tickets 

### Cancelamos el ticket
PATCH http://localhost:9909/api/tickets/6ac99ec09a40431703f63b6a/cancel

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.- Respuesta de /current no incluye password 
GET http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/current

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.- Respuesta de ticket con populate no incluye password del usuario 
GET http://localhost:9909/api/tickets/my-tickets 

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.- Endpoint con error de negocio devuelve código HTTP correcto (no 500)
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/logout

### Me logueo como organizer 
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "organizer2@gmail.com",
    "password": "organizer2_1234"
}

### Intento crear un evento que no cumpla con la logica de negocio 
### (titulo repetido, precio negativo, capacidad menor o igual a 0)
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "evento 2",
    "description": "descripcion del evento 2",
    "category": "categoria 2",
    "date": "2027-02-02",
    "location": "ubicacion 2",
    "capacity": 200,
    "price": 20
}

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5.- Endpoint protegido sin sesión → 401; con sesión sin permisos → 403
### Cerramos sesión
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/logout

### Sin iniciar sesión, intentamos crear un evento
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "evento 3",
    "description": "descripcion del evento 3",
    "category": "categoria 3",
    "date": "2027-03-03",
    "location": "ubicacion 3",
    "capacity": 300,
    "price": 30
}

### Nos logueamos como un usuario e intentamos crear un evento
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login 
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "user1@gmail.com",
    "password": "user1_1234"
}

###
